// A chord ROW leading the system, a two-ending repeat, and a section label at each
// ending's head — the owner's `Lambada Complicada` shape (session 328). Until this session
// the second ending's label was drawn UNDER the bracket, level with the symbols: the
// bracket's floor was measured from the system's top edge (the row's band top, one band
// too high) and the row's symbols were kept out of the outside-staff support, so the
// bracket never met a symbol and the label found a pocket under the hooks.
//
// LilyPond 2.26.0 (audit/lp-geometry/probes/volta-chord-row.ly, book VCR): the bracket's
// line stands on the "Am" under its number by outside-staff-padding 0.46, and both labels
// stand 0.46 over the bracket — ledger page.volta.chord-row.symbol-to-line and
// mark.second-ending.chord-row.line-to-box-bottom. "A", with no symbol under it, keeps its
// plain height beside the first symbol, as LilyPond's does.
time 2/4
part mel {
  clef treble
  section A { c4 d | e f | }
  section E1 { g4 a | b c' | }
  section E2 { a4 g | f e | d c | }
}
chords prog {
  section A { C | G | }
  section E1 { Am | | }
  section E2 { | Dm G | C | }
}
form main { |: A [1. E1 ] :| [2. E2 ] |. }
score main { chords prog staff mel }
